meta {
  name: Complete Agency Setup
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agency/setup/complete
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{onboardOwnerAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "skipped": true
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    // 200, not 201 — this updates a sub-document, it creates nothing.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("marks it complete and records that it was skipped", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().status).to.equal("complete");
    expect(res.getBody().brandingSkipped).to.equal(true);
    expect(res.getBody().completedAt).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /agency/setup/complete — finish the first-run setup (PAC-69)

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `agency:branding:write`
  - **Data scope:** the caller's own agency (`@SkipBranch()`).

  ## Body
  ```json
  { "skipped": true }
  ```

  `skipped` records that the owner pressed "Skip for now" rather than filling
  the white-label step in. **Either way the setup completes** — skipping is a
  decision, and an owner who is not ready to think about logos should not be
  asked again on every sign-in. It is kept because "completed" and "actually
  branded" are different questions, and the second is the one worth a nudge
  later.

  ## Idempotent
  A second call returns the state as it stands rather than conflicting. An owner
  who finishes in two tabs, or re-submits after a flaky response, has done
  nothing wrong, and a 409 there would strand them on the last step of a wizard
  that had already succeeded.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  { "status": "complete", "completedAt": "2026-09-02T…Z", "brandingSkipped": true }
  ```

  Once complete, `/auth/me` reports `agencySetupPending: false` and the app stops
  redirecting the owner to `/welcome/agency`.

  ## Errors
  - `403 Forbidden` — lacks `agency:branding:write`.
}
